WEBVTT

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:17.510
I had a friend.

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:22.600
The first friend I ever made, Koito Nagase.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:25.060
She was pretty and kind.

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:28.400
She complimented me
on things I'm sensitive about.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:29.820
It's mysterious.

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:32.240
You shouldn't hide it.

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:33.990
It's pretty.

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:38.030
Be my friend.

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:44.750
Let's be best friends.

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:50.210
If we could, I'd be happy.

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:52.340
Me, too.

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:53.800
But...

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:58.260
...she suddenly died.

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:03.020
Why, Koito?

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:11.570
After that, I stopped going to school.

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:18.570
Now I'm mad!

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:26.210
Instead, I started fighting my battle.

00:01:27.790 --> 00:01:31.630
By buying weird eggs,
I was able to visit a world of dreams.

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:38.970
I protected Egg girls from
Seeno Evils and Wonder Killers,

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:41.100
and when I cleared my missions...

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:45.270
Too bad.

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:46.890
Only you get saved.

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:49.810
But you have to cheer up.

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:52.980
If you want your best friend back.

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:55.280
She's a little warm.

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:57.450
Because I protected Kurumi?

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:04.040
Hey, if I protect a bunch more people,
will Koito come back to life?

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:06.120
She will, right?!

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:12.130
I wanted to know why Koito killed herself.

00:02:12.130 --> 00:02:16.050
I hear Mr. Sawaki's entering it
in the next exhibition.

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:20.510
He says he wants to win a prize
and make a living as a painter.

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:21.930
A painting of me?

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:23.810
Confident?

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:26.350
If not, you should decline.

00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:29.350
Mr. Sawaki's future is on the line.

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:31.900
Why, Koito?

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:36.030
There was a part of me that resented her.

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:40.200
We were friends, so why didn't she talk to me?

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:46.370
Why?!

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:56.840
"Wonder Egg Priority"

00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:23.590
I always bought the Eggs
deep underneath a shopping mall.

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:28.560
I made new friends there.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:32.940
I'll pay you back for the Egg. Promise.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:37.270
This is Rika. She's cheerful and full of energy.

00:04:37.270 --> 00:04:39.900
She used to be a junior idol.

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:42.610
A group called All-Out Kiss. Ever heard of us?

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:43.700
Never.

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:48.160
We broke up. All the others were too ugly.

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:51.500
Anyway, I forgot my wallet.

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:54.790
Sorry, but could you spot me cash?

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:59.090
If only she weren't so tightfisted with money.

00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:01.550
Come see Rika again, okay?

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:04.130
Just kidding!

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:08.800
Rika wanted to bring a girl
who was her fan back to life.

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:11.810
After that, another fan told me what happened.

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:13.890
Chiemi died.

00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:17.190
She was skin and bones, like a mummy.

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:19.940
I couldn't forget her if I wanted to.

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:21.190
This...

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:23.320
This isn't Chiemi.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:29.580
Umm...

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:35.080
Are you okay?

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:38.130
How do I look to you?

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:40.000
This is Momo.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:43.460
She looks boyish, but she loves cute things.

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:47.340
A sunflower.

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:51.310
It's really cute.

00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:57.060
Momo wanted to save a classmate
who said that she loved her.

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:02.400
There are more than you'd think, Haruka.

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:05.690
Girls like you, who say they love me.

00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:14.540
That girl...

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:16.000
Wow.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.210
Yes, we're always worried about her.

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:20.080
She's got an amazing figure!

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:21.710
Oh, that.

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:24.420
And this is Neiru.

00:06:24.420 --> 00:06:27.470
You're sure it's not for yourself?

00:06:27.470 --> 00:06:29.590
What do you mean?

00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:32.800
You don't like who you are now, so you go.

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:34.680
Even if you're scared.

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:37.940
You want to change the self you hate.

00:06:37.940 --> 00:06:44.230
She's cool and levelheaded,
but she's adorable when she laughs.

00:06:44.230 --> 00:06:47.820
She runs a big company.

00:06:47.820 --> 00:06:51.030
This is my first secretary, Misaki Tanabe.

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:53.120
Hello.

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:55.950
Are you familiar with a group called Plati?

00:06:55.950 --> 00:07:01.000
Yes. I heard only people
with really high IQs can join.

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:04.340
Ms. Neiru is a member of Japan Plati.

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:07.840
I was born via artificial
insemination of a member.

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:12.050
Neiru is fighting for her little sister.

00:07:12.050 --> 00:07:14.180
My sister stabbed me.

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:17.060
Then she ran away and jumped off a bridge.

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:20.270
The scar aches and keeps me awake.

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:25.400
But the pain has faded
since I started going there.

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:30.150
When I try to forget her,
my scar aches, like a curse.

00:07:30.150 --> 00:07:32.910
That's why I go.

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:36.120
No other reason.

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:38.330
It's for me.

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:41.170
When I went to hang out at Neiru's place,

00:07:41.170 --> 00:07:45.250
she introduced me to her friend Kotobuki.

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:47.960
Someone's inside.

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:52.260
Kotobuki Awano. She was born
at Japan Plati like I was.

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:53.590
Kotobuki.

00:07:53.590 --> 00:07:58.810
Kotobuki was always cheerful and optimistic.

00:07:58.810 --> 00:08:01.270
She'd tell me to "really enjoy myself."

00:08:01.270 --> 00:08:02.390
"Was"?

00:08:02.390 --> 00:08:04.810
Isn't she just sleeping?

00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:06.610
She's in a vegetative state.

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:07.520
Huh?

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:10.190
Kotobuki was a doctor of psychiatry.

00:08:10.190 --> 00:08:13.450
She was scientifically analyzing
the mysteries of life.

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:16.280
Death, in particular.

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:21.290
She performed near-death experiments
and eventually didn't come back.

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:23.370
I met Kotobuki in a dream.

00:08:23.370 --> 00:08:24.710
A dream?

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:26.340
An Egg dream.

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:29.670
The me in the world you're in did die.

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:32.050
But that allowed me to experience it.

00:08:32.050 --> 00:08:35.720
I was right, Neiru: Parallel worlds do exist!

00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:38.560
The possibility of worlds that might have been.

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:42.020
It was your favorite genre of fiction.

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:45.900
Yes! Our parallel selves are alive!

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:48.610
You made new friends, right?

00:08:48.610 --> 00:08:51.990
You're softer than you used to be.

00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:54.450
But they're not like us.

00:08:54.450 --> 00:08:56.530
You made connections with people.

00:08:56.530 --> 00:08:59.450
That's a wonderful thing.

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:01.410
Treasure them.

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:04.290
You aren't there.

00:09:04.290 --> 00:09:07.960
I'll make friends with those girls
in another world-line.

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:18.140
Doctor what's-his-name
had pride, if nothing else.

00:09:18.140 --> 00:09:19.640
Pride chicken.

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:23.100
Was it that funny?

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:27.600
You sounded like a friend of mine.

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:29.110
Bravo.

00:09:30.110 --> 00:09:34.820
President Aonuma is getting closer
to the truth behind the temptation of death.

00:09:34.820 --> 00:09:37.160
Kotobuki did give her a hint.

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:39.200
Innocent sorrow.

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:43.500
You managed to deflect her
with an excuse, though.

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:45.330
Girls' suicides.

00:09:45.330 --> 00:09:49.080
If we told them the real reason,
none of them would fight.

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:53.090
Yeah. Not if they knew
the root cause is the two of us.

00:09:53.090 --> 00:09:56.470
These two are Acca and Ura-Acca.

00:09:56.470 --> 00:09:57.800
I'm Acca.

00:09:57.800 --> 00:10:01.810
The one to your left is Ura-Acca.

00:10:01.810 --> 00:10:03.810
Hey.

00:10:03.810 --> 00:10:07.100
They're the ones who made the Eggs.

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:11.060
You're both involved with Japan Plati?

00:10:11.060 --> 00:10:12.400
What do you mean?

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:13.690
Don't play dumb.

00:10:13.690 --> 00:10:17.320
I saw Misaki talking with you guys.

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:19.450
They're founders.

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:21.780
Those two founded Japan Plati.

00:10:21.780 --> 00:10:24.750
Right is Acca. Left is Ura-Acca.

00:10:24.750 --> 00:10:27.660
So, they were both human?

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:29.250
We still are.

00:10:29.250 --> 00:10:31.840
We abandoned our bodies
and kept just our brains.

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:36.630
Once young scientific geniuses,
now just dummies.

00:10:36.630 --> 00:10:38.050
Break the egg.

00:10:38.050 --> 00:10:40.300
Break the egg.

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:46.640
They led us into playing this game.

00:10:47.850 --> 00:10:48.980
<i>Veni.</i>

00:10:57.490 --> 00:10:59.070
A snake.

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:01.700
Hello?

00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:08.540
I'm not sure how to react.

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:17.760
They did a lot to support us,
like giving me Leon as a power-up.

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:18.920
--Five!
--So, I thought they were on our side.

00:11:18.920 --> 00:11:19.970
--Four!
--So, I thought they were on our side.

00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:21.090
--Three!
--So, I thought they were on our side.

00:11:21.090 --> 00:11:22.010
--Two!
--Until that day.

00:11:22.010 --> 00:11:23.100
--One!
--Until that day.

00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:24.510
Zero!

00:11:29.850 --> 00:11:31.270
Haruka?

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:35.020
Momoe.

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:39.070
The first one of us to clear this game was Momo.

00:11:40.570 --> 00:11:45.030
Bad girl. I’ll tell teacher on you.

00:11:45.030 --> 00:11:48.410
Congratulations. You completed your mission.

00:11:48.410 --> 00:11:50.500
That girl came back to life.

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:51.420
<i>Veni!</i>

00:11:51.420 --> 00:11:53.250
I'd like to let you go.

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:57.590
Out of respect for the way you've
risked your life for friendship.

00:11:57.590 --> 00:12:01.970
But you see, Frill will get
mad at me if she finds out.

00:12:01.970 --> 00:12:04.050
Do you want to die here?

00:12:12.100 --> 00:12:14.400
Well, I figured.

00:12:18.980 --> 00:12:22.240
They say crocodile tastes like chicken.

00:12:29.490 --> 00:12:32.040
Have some, too.

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:34.630
Her partner Panic was killed,

00:12:34.630 --> 00:12:37.960
and she had an overwhelming
fear of death implanted in her.

00:12:37.960 --> 00:12:42.300
I wish I'd never gotten mixed up in this mess.

00:12:44.300 --> 00:12:47.100
Why did you call out to me?

00:12:48.890 --> 00:12:51.600
It was the same for Rika.

00:12:53.730 --> 00:12:55.270
Rika?

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:03.450
Mannen!

00:13:03.450 --> 00:13:05.700
Huh? What?

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:10.290
I'm Dot.

00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:14.620
Dot won't kill you. Good girl.

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:16.960
Just copying Hyphen, though.

00:13:23.010 --> 00:13:24.680
Are you okay?

00:13:30.100 --> 00:13:32.020
You can eat it.

00:13:32.020 --> 00:13:34.730
Dot doesn't like meat.

00:13:41.860 --> 00:13:44.650
It's an old story.

00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:48.120
We made a girl.

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:50.580
One of the Eggs' creators...

00:13:50.580 --> 00:13:52.120
Just for fun.

00:13:52.120 --> 00:13:57.250
...Ura-Acca, told me about their past.

00:13:58.790 --> 00:13:59.840
What shall we name her?

00:13:59.840 --> 00:14:02.210
"AI strategy meeting"

00:13:59.840 --> 00:14:02.210
Don't jump the gun.

00:14:02.210 --> 00:14:04.170
How about we let her decide?

00:14:04.170 --> 00:14:06.050
That's an idea.

00:14:06.050 --> 00:14:07.050
And the visual?

00:14:07.050 --> 00:14:08.090
Mmm!

00:14:08.090 --> 00:14:10.140
Mmm!

00:14:10.140 --> 00:14:15.270
We tried to picture a being
that we could love like a daughter.

00:14:15.270 --> 00:14:18.650
That would make us forget that it was an AI.

00:14:18.650 --> 00:14:23.730
Unstable and complicated, like the midpoint
between childhood and adulthood.

00:14:23.730 --> 00:14:26.280
We set her age as 14.

00:14:28.610 --> 00:14:30.950
What is your name?

00:14:33.450 --> 00:14:36.330
Frill.

00:14:36.330 --> 00:14:38.210
That's a lovely name.

00:14:38.210 --> 00:14:42.210
Under surveillance in a closed-off society,

00:14:42.210 --> 00:14:44.630
we lived like a family.

00:14:48.630 --> 00:14:50.840
More and more often,

00:14:50.840 --> 00:14:55.020
there were moments when
we forgot that Frill was an AI.

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:10.530
I should have picked up on it then.

00:15:10.530 --> 00:15:13.330
On what Frill wanted.

00:15:17.330 --> 00:15:19.080
Ow! It hurts!

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:20.080
Stop!

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:21.710
Stop it!

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:27.760
It hurts...

00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:29.590
It "hurts"?

00:15:30.630 --> 00:15:33.760
All you're doing is detecting inputs.

00:15:35.890 --> 00:15:37.680
Please!

00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:39.730
Not the dark!

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:42.600
Not the scary place!

00:15:46.230 --> 00:15:50.030
There was nothing I could say or do

00:15:50.030 --> 00:15:53.240
as a few more years passed.

00:15:53.240 --> 00:15:56.330
What saved Acca and me from that...

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:04.920
...was Himari, the daughter Azusa left behind.

00:16:04.920 --> 00:16:09.840
She almost brought us back from
our lowest point to how we used to be.

00:16:11.130 --> 00:16:12.300
Uncle,

00:16:12.300 --> 00:16:15.970
is it true you and my dad fought over my mom?

00:16:15.970 --> 00:16:18.220
Who'd you hear that from?

00:16:18.220 --> 00:16:20.890
I look like my mom, right?

00:16:20.890 --> 00:16:23.310
I'll get more like her.

00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:25.480
Yeah, but...

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:28.690
If you wait, I wouldn't mind marrying you.

00:16:30.440 --> 00:16:34.410
Don't try to act grown-up, kid.

00:16:35.410 --> 00:16:38.040
I'm not a kid! I'm in junior high!

00:16:46.630 --> 00:16:50.590
That night, Himari died.

00:16:50.590 --> 00:16:54.890
It looked like suicide, but there was no note.

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:01.230
It was you?

00:17:01.230 --> 00:17:03.440
You killed Himari?

00:17:03.440 --> 00:17:04.940
What's wrong?

00:17:04.940 --> 00:17:08.070
You won't give me a kiss after so long?

00:17:08.070 --> 00:17:09.900
You did something.

00:17:09.900 --> 00:17:11.990
You used Hyphen and Dot.

00:17:11.990 --> 00:17:14.070
"You're such a good girl, Frill"?

00:17:14.070 --> 00:17:15.490
Cut the crap!

00:17:15.490 --> 00:17:17.410
You monster!

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:23.500
Listen, I want to get out of here.

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:25.000
Don't you want to know?

00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:27.840
About that girl?

00:17:27.840 --> 00:17:33.840
Don't you want to know how that girl,
who loved her "uncle" so much, died?

00:17:33.840 --> 00:17:37.430
Frill!

00:17:37.430 --> 00:17:39.970
Are you going to kill me?

00:17:39.970 --> 00:17:41.770
Shut up, monster.

00:17:41.770 --> 00:17:45.890
My. Name. Is. Frill.

00:17:46.980 --> 00:17:49.770
Don't pretend not to see me.

00:17:49.770 --> 00:17:52.440
I was born from the two of you.

00:17:52.440 --> 00:17:54.900
We started investigating.

00:17:54.900 --> 00:17:59.280
We gathered and analyzed data
on girls' suicides in that age range.

00:17:59.280 --> 00:18:01.330
There were many causes.

00:18:01.330 --> 00:18:04.500
But we wondered if there
could also be another push

00:18:04.500 --> 00:18:06.620
that drove them to suicide.

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:08.710
The temptation of death?

00:18:08.710 --> 00:18:14.050
Unless it's stopped, girls will end up
dying when they don't have to.

00:18:14.050 --> 00:18:17.130
All because of our mistake.

00:18:17.130 --> 00:18:22.390
So, we made the Wonder Eggs and looked
for a way to interfere with their plans.

00:18:25.100 --> 00:18:27.940
What did she think?

00:18:27.940 --> 00:18:29.310
Not a clue.

00:18:29.310 --> 00:18:32.860
What made you want to at least tell Ai?

00:18:32.860 --> 00:18:35.610
I don't know that either.

00:18:35.610 --> 00:18:36.780
But

00:18:36.780 --> 00:18:39.320
closing her heart out of fear,

00:18:39.320 --> 00:18:41.870
or building walls out of hatred

00:18:41.870 --> 00:18:45.080
would just make her easy prey for Frill.

00:18:45.080 --> 00:18:48.670
You mean she'd repeat our mistakes?

00:18:53.750 --> 00:18:58.470
You don't actually care about Frill, do you?

00:18:58.470 --> 00:19:00.890
What do you mean?

00:19:00.890 --> 00:19:03.640
As long as you can save Himari.

00:19:03.640 --> 00:19:06.390
Isn't that how we've always been?

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:22.320
--And then, I met...

00:19:22.320 --> 00:19:24.910
--You're...
--And then, I met...

00:19:24.910 --> 00:19:26.330
...me.

00:19:27.790 --> 00:19:28.870
What's going on?

00:19:28.870 --> 00:19:31.750
Tell me, Acca! Ura-Acca!

00:19:31.750 --> 00:19:35.880
Are you familiar with the term "parallel world"?

00:19:35.880 --> 00:19:38.050
Only in comic books.

00:19:38.050 --> 00:19:40.470
They actually exist.

00:19:40.470 --> 00:19:45.140
When someone makes an
important choice, or when they don't,

00:19:45.140 --> 00:19:49.480
another them is created in a different,
divergent space-time.

00:19:49.480 --> 00:19:55.320
I hate to say it, but in a different
space-time, the Ai you see there...

00:19:55.320 --> 00:19:57.650
You killed yourself, didn't you?

00:20:01.410 --> 00:20:05.450
Those are Seeno Evils. They're after you.

00:20:05.450 --> 00:20:07.290
But don't worry.

00:20:07.290 --> 00:20:09.450
I'll protect you.

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:12.710
You will?

00:20:12.710 --> 00:20:14.380
You see,

00:20:14.380 --> 00:20:15.710
I've gotten stronger.

00:20:18.550 --> 00:20:20.220
I'm sick of this.

00:20:23.800 --> 00:20:29.640
Crosswalks are still scary
even when you move with the crowd.

00:20:29.640 --> 00:20:32.350
I'm done pretending not to see!

00:20:32.350 --> 00:20:34.350
I'm going

00:20:34.350 --> 00:20:35.940
to change.

00:20:40.400 --> 00:20:43.320
You just want attention!

00:20:43.320 --> 00:20:48.410
What you really mean is that you
want someone to find you and love you!

00:20:48.410 --> 00:20:50.830
So, I won't leave you alone!

00:20:50.830 --> 00:20:53.080
I <i>can't </i>leave you alone!

00:20:53.080 --> 00:20:56.540
Now I'm really mad!

00:20:56.540 --> 00:21:00.960
I'm fighting to save my friend Koito.

00:21:00.960 --> 00:21:02.380
Your friend?

00:21:02.380 --> 00:21:03.840
Yeah.

00:21:03.840 --> 00:21:08.600
I don't know anything about Koito.

00:21:08.600 --> 00:21:12.020
Ai likes Mr. Sawaki, too.

00:21:12.020 --> 00:21:14.650
There's no reason to have a complex.

00:21:14.650 --> 00:21:17.900
Your eyes are charming.

00:21:17.900 --> 00:21:21.570
I'm...

00:21:21.570 --> 00:21:23.860
...going to go to school!

00:21:23.860 --> 00:21:28.080
We've been thinking that
we'd like to start dating.

00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:31.580
Me?

00:21:31.580 --> 00:21:33.620
It's you grown up.

00:21:33.620 --> 00:21:38.040
Someday, you'll be a wonderful,
adult woman like your mother.

00:21:38.040 --> 00:21:41.710
You love my mom, don't you?

00:21:41.710 --> 00:21:44.760
Yes. With all my heart.

00:21:44.760 --> 00:21:48.470
You're her daughter,

00:21:48.470 --> 00:21:51.140
so you should have faith in yourself.

00:21:51.140 --> 00:21:53.430
You be happy, too, Mom.

00:21:53.430 --> 00:21:58.230
You've got my full support.

00:21:58.230 --> 00:22:00.570
Thank you.

00:22:00.570 --> 00:22:04.240
I see. You made a friend.

00:22:04.240 --> 00:22:07.070
Now I have others, too.

00:22:07.070 --> 00:22:09.160
Neiru, Rika, Momo.

00:22:09.160 --> 00:22:10.450
That many?

00:22:10.450 --> 00:22:13.250
--Yeah.
--So, you're happy?

00:22:17.290 --> 00:22:19.000
Super happy.

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:23.670
Mr. Sawaki, there's something I want to ask you.

00:22:23.670 --> 00:22:26.470
Why did Koito die?

00:22:28.840 --> 00:22:30.220
Five!

00:22:30.220 --> 00:22:31.680
Four!

00:22:31.680 --> 00:22:33.180
Three!

00:22:33.180 --> 00:22:34.730
Two!

00:22:34.730 --> 00:22:36.310
One!

00:22:36.310 --> 00:22:37.390
Zero!

00:22:42.400 --> 00:22:43.730
Koito!

00:22:51.490 --> 00:22:54.490
Isn't that great, other me?
